# --- data: all regenerable via download_demo + replay_trajectory -------------
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.zarr/
demos/
maniskill_data/
data/
*.pkl
*.npz

# ...but keep the metadata JSONs that document what the demos were.
!**/trajectory.json

# --- model artifacts ---------------------------------------------------------
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
checkpoints/*
runs/

# ...with exactly one exception: the frozen base policy, committed on purpose
# so the T-II harness runs with no env var and no rsync from a dead pod. 33 MB,
# ema_agent only. See checkpoints/README.md.
#
# The negations are narrow BY NAME, not a blanket !checkpoints/*.pt - a training
# run writes best_eval_success_at_end.pt beside it, and 'nothing large goes into
# git' has no cheap undo once it is in history.
!checkpoints/stackcube_rgb_spatial_800demos.pt
!checkpoints/README.md

# ...and one more: the T-IV residual heads. Same argument as the base policy -
# they are the T-IV deliverable, the weights every after-number came from, and
# `runs/` above would otherwise swallow them exactly as `checkpoints/*` swallowed
# the whole of T-III's generated output. ~1.7 MB each (416k params), six of them.
#
# NARROW BY NAME again: train_ppo.py writes only residual_seed<n>.pt into this
# directory, so a stray checkpoint or a wandb dump beside it stays ignored.
!t4/runs/
!t4/runs/*/
!t4/runs/*/residual_seed?.pt
!t4/runs/*/*_train.csv
!t4/runs/*/*_manifest.json
t4/runs/smoke/
outputs/
logs/

# --- experiment tracking -----------------------------------------------------
wandb/
lightning_logs/
tensorboard/
events.out.tfevents.*

# --- media -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rollout videos go in the submission zip, not in git. Binary, large, and they
# bloat history permanently. Keep them in videos/ locally so the zip step is
# a straight copy.
*.mp4
*.avi
*.gif
*.webm
videos/

# figures/ (analyze_rollouts.py's output) IS committed - the plots are small,
# they are report deliverables, and they want versioning alongside the code that
# made them. No rule is needed: nothing above ignores *.png or *.pdf, so they
# are tracked by omission. Said here because silence about a committed artifact
# type reads like an oversight - the same reason the T-II block below exists.

# --- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM API keys for T-III, wandb key, R2/S3 credentials.
#
# The T-III key lives OUTSIDE the repo entirely, at $RIPL_ROOT/anthropic.env
# (chmod 600), which t3/run.sh sources if present. Not in env.sh: that file is
# rewritten by every setup_runpod.sh run and echoed into build logs.
.env
.env.*
*.key
secrets.yaml
credentials*
.aws/

# --- python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
venv/
.venv/
env/
.python-version
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- os / editor -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# --- runpod / container scratch ----------------------------------------------
vulkaninfo.txt
ENVIRONMENT.txt
smoke/
nohup.out

# --- generated environment ----------------------------------------------------
# setup_runpod.sh writes env.sh to $RIPL_ROOT, outside this repo, so this is
# belt-and-braces against a copy landing here. CLAUDE.md claims it is covered.
env.sh

# T-II rollout data, committed deliberately.
#
# The mined CSVs are a few MB and are the evidence base for the failure-mode
# characterisation, so they belong in the repo. *.csv is not matched by
# anything above, so they are already tracked - no rule needed, but say so
# here, because silence about the one data type this project DOES commit reads
# like an oversight.
#
# The .npz sidecars (per-episode traces, initial/terminal sim states) are
# caught by the blanket *.npz on line 9, so they need an explicit exception.
# They are what make the analysis reproducible from the repo alone, without a
# working ManiSkill install. Tens of MB, which is the ceiling for this - if a
# trace pass ever gets much bigger than that, keep it on the pod and pull it
# instead, per CLAUDE.md's rule that nothing large goes into git.
!*_states.npz
!*_trace.npz

# --- T-III artifacts ---------------------------------------------------------
# t3/artifacts/**/ holds the committed evidence for the LLM pipeline: the exact
# assembled prompt, the frames the model was shown, the raw API response, the
# generated reward.py and sampler.py, and the validation output. All of it is
# small, all of it is a deliverable ("document the prompt(s) you used"), and a
# REJECTED generation is kept too - which check caught it is the report's
# account of how an LLM-written reward fails. .jpg and .json are tracked by
# omission; this comment exists so nobody adds a blanket rule that catches them.
#
# t3/results/ holds the measurements check.py writes and summary.py reads.

# mp4s stay ignored (*.mp4 above). Reference them from the report; they are
# regenerable from a seed with record_seeds.py.
